{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p20-7b25a77e","text":"All done. Let me write the final summary covering both the landing page redesign and the Acadex rename.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"}
The landing page is redesigned and everything is now branded **Acadex**.

**Landing page rebuild** — [LandingPage.tsx](frontend/src/features/marketing/LandingPage.tsx) and [landing.css](frontend/src/shared/styles/landing.css) were rewritten from scratch:

- **Hero**: trust badge, tighter headline typography, dual CTAs, and a full app mockup (browser chrome, sidebar nav, four stat cards with pastel chips, an attendance bar chart, and a timetable list) instead of the old sparse box
- **New sections**: a "who it's for" role strip, a nine-card feature grid using the same pastel chip palette as the app (`#eef3ff`, `#e7f7ef`, `#f2edfc`, `#fdf3e2`, `#fdeceb`), two alternating showcase blocks with working mini-mockups (attendance roster and report card), a three-step onboarding row with dashed connectors, a stats band, an expanded security section with a gradient card, a gradient CTA band, and a proper multi-column footer
- **Polish**: sticky blurred nav, hover states, focus-visible rings, skip link, `prefers-reduced-motion` support, and breakpoints at 1100/820/560px — hamburger menu verified on mobile at 390px

**Acadex rename** — every user-visible occurrence across 11 files: landing page, login/register pages, invitation page, app sidebar, settings, report cards, teaching assignments, page title/meta/OG tags, the FastAPI docs title, and the [README](README.md). I deliberately left the internal identifiers alone (`schoolos_csrf` cookie name, Redis key prefixes, the TOTP encryption AAD, DB name) — those are invisible to users, and changing cookies/2FA would sign everyone out and break existing authenticator secrets.

**Verified**: TypeScript passes, both containers rebuilt and healthy, and I walked the full page top to bottom in the browser on desktop and mobile — no console errors from the new code (the logged 401s are the normal signed-out session check).

One note: the signup form's workspace prefix now shows `acadex.app/` — say the word if your real domain differs and I'll adjust it.

Want me to carry the Acadex branding into the README's setup instructions next, or adjust the landing copy/sections further?

